                            POSITION RECOVERY • HOMING • JAM CLEARING • HMI INTERFACE

========================================================================================================================
 Project:       Roller Door PLC Program
 Description:   Automatic opening and closing with position control,
                jam detection, jam clearing, homing, auto-commisioning and PAR-5 HMI supported
 Author:        Max Placidi
 Version:       1.5
 Date:          04/08/2026

 Program Sections
 1. Track limit detection
 2. Jam detection     
 3. Loading parameters
 4. Parameter box display and information
 5. State machine
 6. Fault clearing
 7. Homing 
 8. Movement, power and current position assignment saving

========================================================================================================================

PARAMETER OVERWRITES:
P480[09] = Reference point [23]
P481[09] = Output via PLC  [40]

ADJUSTABLE PARAMETERS:
P355[01] = Variable - RunFreq                                           [Test value: 2000]  Fraction out of 16384
P355[02] = Variable - ClearFreq                                         [Test value: 3500]  Fraction out of 16384
P355[03] = Variable - TorqueLimitUp                                     [Test value: 2]     Unit is deciamps
P355[04] = Variable - TorqueLimitDown                                   [Test value: 2]     Unit is deciamps
P355[05] = Variable - MaxJams                                           [Test value: 5]
P355[06] = Variable - HomeFreq                                          [Test value: 2000]  Fraction out of 16384
P355[07] = Variable - FloorDeadZone                                     [Test value: 100]   Unit is millirevs
P355[08] = Variable - TopDeadZone                                       [Test value: 100]   Unit is millirevs
P355[09] = Variable - HomingTorqueLimit                                 [Test value: 2]     Unit is deciamps
P355[10] = Variable - ConfigSelect (preset number 1..8)

P356[01] = Last saved position. Loaded in during drive initialisation   [Test value: 100]   Unit is millirevs
P356[02] = Variable - EndPos                                            [Test value: 10000] Unit is millirevs
P356[03] = Variable - RestTime                                          [Test value: 2000]  Unit is milliseconds
P356[04] = Variable - JamTime                                           [Test value: 2000]  Unit is milliseconds

Assumes top sensor is digital input 5 
And bottom is         digital input 6

CONTROLS:
DI1 OR Parameter box up: Door open
DI2 OR Parameter box down: Force door closed OR Reference point during homing
DI5: Test jam signal
DI6 OR (Parameter box ok + Parameter box on): Initiate homing

ERRORS:
E23 Flag 1: Max jam clearing attempts reached.
    Flag 2: DI5 triggered (top sensor)
    Flag 3: DI6 triggered (bottom sensor)
========================================================================================================================*)

(* *************************************************************** *)
(*                          MAIN PROGRAM                           *)
(* *************************************************************** *)

(* Version 1.1 - save/preset repair and memory reduction (unvalidated draft)
   - One parameter-write sequencer: SavePar16 and SavePar32 are each driven from one place.
     HMI edits write one parameter; presets write P355[01..10] and P356[02..04].
   - Write errors no longer stall the sequencer; EXECUTE drops for one scan between steps.
   - Preset CASE runs once per request (no longer re-armed every scan).
   - Parameter reload is held off while a write sequence is running, so presets are not
     overwritten by old parameter values before being saved.
   - Presets: common values first, then each CASE entry overrides only what differs.
   - ParamInit RAM writes run once per PLC start (MUX tables instead of CASE).
   - Page 4 reduced to the preset selector row only.
   - LoadConf is a one-shot command: presets apply when selection > 0, then P355[10] is saved as 0.
   - Removed the continuous floor-position Init reset that restarted ParamInit and blocked edits.
   Not compiled or commissioned. Check PLC memory use in NORDCON after compiling.
   Reference: NORD BU 0550 4.3.3.15 (pp.77-78), 4.4.1.6/4.4.1.9 (pp.121-123), 4.8 (pp.181-184).
*)

(*1. --------------------Track Limit detection----------------------*)
DI5Edge(CLK:=_5_State_digital_input.4);  (*Top sensor*)
DI6Edge(CLK:=_5_State_digital_input.5);  (*Bottom sensor*)

IF NOT IsHoming THEN
        IF DI5Edge.Q THEN
                _110_ErrorFlags.1 := TRUE;  (*Exceeded top*)
        END_IF;
        IF DI6Edge.Q THEN
                _110_ErrorFlags.2 := TRUE;  (*Exceeded bottom*)
        END_IF;
END_IF;

(*2. ------------------------Jam detection-----------------------------*)
IF ((_90_Actual_torque_current > TorqueLimitUp)
OR (_90_Actual_torque_current < -TorqueLimitDown))
AND NOT IsHoming AND Power THEN

        (*Jamming when opening, or when re-opening during jam clearing*)
        IF (State = 1)
        OR (((State = 4) OR (State = 6)) AND (_90_Actual_torque_current > 0)) THEN
                JamTimer(IN := FALSE);
                MoveExecute := FALSE;
                JamCount := JamCount + 1;
                IF State = 1 THEN
                        State := 5; (*Clear jam after going up*)
                ELSE
                        State := 6; (*Clear jam after clearing a jam while going up*)
                END_IF;

        (*Jamming when closing*)
        ELSIF (State = 3) AND (_90_Actual_torque_current < 0) THEN
                JamCount := JamCount + 1;
                SetFreq := ClearFreq;
                MoveExecute := FALSE;
                Power := FALSE;
                State := 4; (*Clear jam after going down*)
        END_IF;
END_IF;

(*3. --------------------Loading parameters---------------------*)
IF NOT Init THEN
        (*Reload only when no parameter write sequence is running*)
        IF ConfigInit = 0 THEN
                EndPos := _126_PLC_P356_2;
                TargetPos := EndPos;
                MoveExecute := FALSE;
                Power := FALSE;

                (*Restores position from memory*)
                IF (_125_PLC_P356_1 > FloorDeadZone)
                AND (_125_PLC_P356_1 < (EndPos - TopDeadZone)) THEN
                        ResetPos(EXECUTE := TRUE, POSITION := _125_PLC_P356_1);
                END_IF;

                RestTime := _127_PLC_P356_3;
                JamTime := _128_PLC_P356_4;
                RunFreq := _115_PLC_P355_1;
                ClearFreq := _116_PLC_P355_2;
                TorqueLimitUp := _117_PLC_P355_3;
                TorqueLimitDown := _118_PLC_P355_4;
                MaxJams := _119_PLC_P355_5;
                HomeFreq := _120_PLC_P355_6;
                FloorDeadZone := INT_TO_DINT(_121_PLC_P355_7);
                TopDeadZone := INT_TO_DINT(_122_PLC_P355_8);
                HomingTorqueLimit := _123_PLC_P355_9;
                ConfigSelect := _124_PLC_P355_10;

                (*LoadConf is a command register: clear an old nonzero value on startup.
                  A blank drive instead loads the default preset, whose final write clears it.*)
                IF _126_PLC_P356_2 <= 0 THEN
                        ConfigSelect := 1;
                        ConfigInit := 20;
                ELSIF ConfigSelect <> 0 THEN
                        ConfigSelect := 0;
                        ConfigInit := 13;
                END_IF;

                Init := TRUE;
        END_IF;
ELSE
        (*Writing position; paused while the save sequencer is writing*)
        WritePos(
                EXECUTE := (State <> 0) AND (ConfigInit = 0) AND (WriterPhase = 0) AND (ParamInit = 0) AND NOT IsEditing,
                PARAMETERNUMBER := 356,
                PARAMETERINDEX := 0,
                VALUE := _145_Actual_pos,
                RAMONLY := 0
        );
        IF WritePos.Done OR WritePos.Error THEN
                WritePos(EXECUTE := FALSE);
        END_IF;
END_IF;

(*RAM-only drive set-up, once per PLC start (ParamInit init value = 1)
  Step: 1      2      3     4      5      6
  Par:  P480   P481   P600  P553   P553   P553
  Idx:  [09]   [09]   [01]  [01]   [02]   [03]
  Val:  23     40     2     1      21     22  *)
IF ParamInit > 0 THEN
        WriteParam(
                EXECUTE := TRUE,
                PARAMETERNUMBER := MUX(ParamInit - 1, 480, 481, 600, 553, 553, 553),
                PARAMETERINDEX := MUX(ParamInit - 1, 8, 8, 0, 0, 1, 2),
                VALUE := MUX(ParamInit - 1, 23, 40, 2, 1, 21, 22),
                RAMONLY := 1
        );
        IF WriteParam.Done OR WriteParam.Error THEN
                WriteParam(EXECUTE := FALSE);
                IF ParamInit >= 6 THEN
                        ParamInit := 0;
                ELSE
                        ParamInit := ParamInit + 1;
                END_IF;
        END_IF;
END_IF;

(*Preset loading: each selection assigns a complete independent parameter set.
  The following values are the defaults already present in the supplied draft;
  replace individual values with the commissioned settings for each door.
  Every valid selection starts the same serialized save list: P355[01..10] and P356[02..04].*)
IF ConfigInit = 20 THEN
        CASE ConfigSelect OF
                1: (*Test configuration*)
                        RunFreq := 2000;
                        ClearFreq := 3500;
                        TorqueLimitUp := 2;
                        TorqueLimitDown := 2;
                        MaxJams := 5;
                        HomeFreq := 2000;
                        FloorDeadZone := 100;
                        TopDeadZone := 100;
                        HomingTorqueLimit := 2;
                        EndPos := 10000;
                        RestTime := 2000;
                        JamTime := 2000;
                        SaveOne := FALSE;
                        ConfigInit := 1;

                2: (*Door 2*)
                        RunFreq := 2000;
                        ClearFreq := 3500;
                        TorqueLimitUp := 2;
                        TorqueLimitDown := 2;
                        MaxJams := 5;
                        HomeFreq := 2000;
                        FloorDeadZone := 100;
                        TopDeadZone := 100;
                        HomingTorqueLimit := 2;
                        EndPos := 10000;
                        RestTime := 2000;
                        JamTime := 2000;
                        SaveOne := FALSE;
                        ConfigInit := 1;

                3: (*Door 3*)
                        RunFreq := 2000;
                        ClearFreq := 3500;
                        TorqueLimitUp := 2;
                        TorqueLimitDown := 2;
                        MaxJams := 5;
                        HomeFreq := 2000;
                        FloorDeadZone := 100;
                        TopDeadZone := 100;
                        HomingTorqueLimit := 2;
                        EndPos := 10000;
                        RestTime := 2000;
                        JamTime := 2000;
                        SaveOne := FALSE;
                        ConfigInit := 1;

                4: (*Door 4*)
                        RunFreq := 2000;
                        ClearFreq := 3500;
                        TorqueLimitUp := 2;
                        TorqueLimitDown := 2;
                        MaxJams := 5;
                        HomeFreq := 2000;
                        FloorDeadZone := 100;
                        TopDeadZone := 100;
                        HomingTorqueLimit := 2;
                        EndPos := 10000;
                        RestTime := 2000;
                        JamTime := 2000;
                        SaveOne := FALSE;
                        ConfigInit := 1;

                5: (*Door 5*)
                        RunFreq := 2000;
                        ClearFreq := 3500;
                        TorqueLimitUp := 2;
                        TorqueLimitDown := 2;
                        MaxJams := 5;
                        HomeFreq := 2000;
                        FloorDeadZone := 100;
                        TopDeadZone := 100;
                        HomingTorqueLimit := 2;
                        EndPos := 10000;
                        RestTime := 2000;
                        JamTime := 2000;
                        SaveOne := FALSE;
                        ConfigInit := 1;
                        
        ELSE
                (*Invalid selector: do not start a preset write sequence.*)
                ConfigSelect := 0;
                ConfigInit := 0;
        END_CASE;

        IF ConfigInit = 1 THEN
                TargetPos := EndPos;
        END_IF;
END_IF;


(*Parameter save sequencer. One FB call per scan and one latched value per request.
  Steps 1-9 -> P355[01..09] (indexes 0..8); steps 10-12 -> P356[02..04]
  (indexes 1..3); step 13 -> P355[10] (index 9), written as zero to re-arm LoadConf.
  WriterPhase 0 prepares,
  1 waits for DONE/ERROR, 2 supplies a full EXECUTE-low scan before advancing.*)
WriterReleaseScan := (WriterPhase = 2);

IF (WriterPhase = 0) AND (ConfigInit >= 1) AND (ConfigInit <= 13)
AND (ParamInit = 0) AND NOT WritePos.Busy THEN
        IF SaveOne THEN
                SaveValue := EditBuffer;
        ELSE
                CASE ConfigInit OF
                        1:  SaveValue := INT_TO_DINT(RunFreq);
                        2:  SaveValue := INT_TO_DINT(ClearFreq);
                        3:  SaveValue := INT_TO_DINT(TorqueLimitUp);
                        4:  SaveValue := INT_TO_DINT(TorqueLimitDown);
                        5:  SaveValue := INT_TO_DINT(MaxJams);
                        6:  SaveValue := INT_TO_DINT(HomeFreq);
                        7:  SaveValue := FloorDeadZone;
                        8:  SaveValue := TopDeadZone;
                        9:  SaveValue := INT_TO_DINT(HomingTorqueLimit);
                        10: SaveValue := EndPos;
                        11: SaveValue := RestTime;
                        12: SaveValue := JamTime;
                        13: SaveValue := 0; (*Clear P355[10] LoadConf command*)
                END_CASE;
        END_IF;

        IF (ConfigInit <= 9) OR (ConfigInit = 13) THEN
                SaveIs32 := FALSE;
                IF ConfigInit = 13 THEN
                        SaveIndex := 9; (*P355[10], zero-based index 9*)
                ELSE
                        SaveIndex := ConfigInit - 1;
                END_IF;
        ELSE
                SaveIs32 := TRUE;
                SaveIndex := ConfigInit - 9;
        END_IF;

        SaveFailed := FALSE;
        WriterPhase := 1;
END_IF;

(*Each parameter FB is called exactly once per scan. The inactive-width FB is held low.*)
SavePar16(
        EXECUTE := (WriterPhase = 1) AND NOT SaveIs32,
        PARAMETERNUMBER := 355,
        PARAMETERINDEX := SaveIndex,
        VALUE := DINT_TO_INT(SaveValue),
        RAMONLY := 0
);

SavePar32(
        EXECUTE := (WriterPhase = 1) AND SaveIs32,
        PARAMETERNUMBER := 356,
        PARAMETERINDEX := SaveIndex,
        VALUE := SaveValue,
        RAMONLY := 0
);

IF (WriterPhase = 1) AND (SavePar16.Done OR SavePar32.Done) THEN
        WriterPhase := 2;
ELSIF (WriterPhase = 1) AND (SavePar16.Error OR SavePar32.Error) THEN
        SaveFailed := TRUE;
        WriterPhase := 2;
END_IF;

IF WriterReleaseScan THEN
        (*The FBs received EXECUTE=FALSE during this scan; now consume the result.*)
        IF SaveFailed THEN
                ConfigInit := 0;
                SaveOne := FALSE;
                Init := FALSE; (*Reload actual stored values after a failed write*)
        ELSIF SaveOne THEN
                (*Update the live variable only after the drive confirms the write.*)
                CASE ConfigInit OF
                        1: RunFreq := DINT_TO_INT(SaveValue);
                        2: ClearFreq := DINT_TO_INT(SaveValue);
                        3: TorqueLimitUp := DINT_TO_INT(SaveValue);
                        4: TorqueLimitDown := DINT_TO_INT(SaveValue);
                        5: MaxJams := DINT_TO_INT(SaveValue);
                        6: HomeFreq := DINT_TO_INT(SaveValue);
                        7: FloorDeadZone := SaveValue;
                        8: TopDeadZone := SaveValue;
                        9: HomingTorqueLimit := DINT_TO_INT(SaveValue);
                        10: EndPos := SaveValue;
                        11: RestTime := SaveValue;
                        12: JamTime := SaveValue;
                        13: ConfigSelect := DINT_TO_INT(SaveValue);
                END_CASE;
                ConfigInit := 0;
                SaveOne := FALSE;
        ELSIF ConfigInit >= 13 THEN
                ConfigInit := 0;
                ConfigSelect := 0; (*Displayed selector returns to idle after preset is saved*)
        ELSE
                ConfigInit := ConfigInit + 1;
        END_IF;
        WriterPhase := 0;
END_IF;

(*4. ----------------------------Display and information--------------------------------*)

(*All key edges from the same process-image snapshot*)
KeyRise := _72_Parameterbox_key_state AND NOT PreviousKeys;
PreviousKeys := _72_Parameterbox_key_state;

IF KeyRise.6 AND (Page <= 0) THEN
        Page := ABS(Page);
        ClearDisplay := TRUE;
END_IF;

IF KeyRise.7 AND (Page >= 1) THEN
        Page := -ABS(Page);
        ClearDisplay := TRUE;
END_IF;

(*ParameterBox scroll repeat: one immediate step, then a delayed repeat.*)
ScrollUpEvent := FALSE;
ScrollDownEvent := FALSE;

IF (Page > 0) AND NOT IsEditing THEN
        IF _72_Parameterbox_key_state.3 AND NOT _72_Parameterbox_key_state.4 THEN
                IF KeyRise.3 THEN
                        ScrollUpEvent := TRUE;
                END_IF;

                IF ScrollDirection <> -1 THEN
                        ScrollDirection := -1;
                        ScrollRepeatActive := FALSE;
                        ScrollTimer(IN := FALSE, PT := ScrollInitialTime);
                ELSIF ScrollTimer.Q THEN
                        ScrollUpEvent := TRUE;
                        ScrollRepeatActive := TRUE;
                        ScrollTimer(IN := FALSE, PT := ScrollRepeatTime);
                ELSIF ScrollRepeatActive THEN
                        ScrollTimer(IN := TRUE, PT := ScrollRepeatTime);
                ELSE
                        ScrollTimer(IN := TRUE, PT := ScrollInitialTime);
                END_IF;

        ELSIF _72_Parameterbox_key_state.4 AND NOT _72_Parameterbox_key_state.3 THEN
                IF KeyRise.4 THEN
                        ScrollDownEvent := TRUE;
                END_IF;

                IF ScrollDirection <> 1 THEN
                        ScrollDirection := 1;
                        ScrollRepeatActive := FALSE;
                        ScrollTimer(IN := FALSE, PT := ScrollInitialTime);
                ELSIF ScrollTimer.Q THEN
                        ScrollDownEvent := TRUE;
                        ScrollRepeatActive := TRUE;
                        ScrollTimer(IN := FALSE, PT := ScrollRepeatTime);
                ELSIF ScrollRepeatActive THEN
                        ScrollTimer(IN := TRUE, PT := ScrollRepeatTime);
                ELSE
                        ScrollTimer(IN := TRUE, PT := ScrollInitialTime);
                END_IF;
        ELSE
                ScrollDirection := 0;
                ScrollRepeatActive := FALSE;
                ScrollTimer(IN := FALSE, PT := ScrollInitialTime);
        END_IF;
ELSE
        ScrollDirection := 0;
        ScrollRepeatActive := FALSE;
        ScrollTimer(IN := FALSE, PT := ScrollInitialTime);
END_IF;

(*Common numeric-display inputs*)
PBoxValue.MODE := BYTE#0;
PBoxValue.COLUMN := BYTE#12;
PBoxValue.POINT := BYTE#0;
PBoxValue.LENGTH := BYTE#6;

(*Each parameter row is drawn left to right: the label string, the live value,
  a unit or percent sign, then an end character that acts as a scroll bar.
  The same four entries are repeated on every row.*)
CASE Page OF
        1: (*RunFreq, ClearFreq, TorqueLimitUp, TorqueLimitDown*)
                (*
                        Line 1: Running frequency
                        Line 2: Frequency used to pull the door up after a jam while closing
                        Line 3: Torque current limit for faults going up
                        Line 4: Torque current limit for faults going down
                *)
                PBoxText(ENABLE := L1Enabled, CLEAR := ClearDisplay, ROW := 0, COLUMN := 0,
                        TEXT := RunFreqStr);
                PBoxValue(ENABLE := L1Enabled, ROW := 0,
                        VALUE := INT_TO_DINT(RunFreq) * 100000 / 16384000);
                PBoxText(ENABLE := TRUE, CLEAR := ClearDisplay, ROW := 0, COLUMN := 18,
                        TEXT := PercentChar);
                PBoxText(ENABLE := TRUE, CLEAR := ClearDisplay, ROW := 0, COLUMN := 19,
                        TEXT := EndChar);

                PBoxText(ENABLE := L2Enabled, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := 1, COLUMN := 0,
                        TEXT := ClearFreqStr);
                PBoxValue(ENABLE := L2Enabled, ROW := 1,
                        VALUE := INT_TO_DINT(ClearFreq) * 100000 / 16384000);
                PBoxText(ENABLE := TRUE, CLEAR := ClearDisplay, ROW := 1, COLUMN := 18,
                        TEXT := PercentChar);
                PBoxText(ENABLE := TRUE, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := 1, COLUMN := 19,
                        TEXT := MidChar);

                PBoxText(ENABLE := L3Enabled, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := 2, COLUMN := 0,
                        TEXT := TorqueLimitUpStr);
                PBoxValue(ENABLE := L3Enabled, ROW := 2,
                        VALUE := INT_TO_DINT(TorqueLimitUp));
                PBoxText(ENABLE := TRUE, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := 2, COLUMN := 19,
                        TEXT := MidChar);

                PBoxText(ENABLE := L4Enabled, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := 3, COLUMN := 0,
                        TEXT := TorqueLimitDownStr);
                PBoxValue(ENABLE := L4Enabled, ROW := 3,
                        VALUE := INT_TO_DINT(TorqueLimitDown));
                PBoxText(ENABLE := TRUE, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := 3, COLUMN := 19,
                        TEXT := DownArrowChar);

                Line1Val := INT_TO_DINT(RunFreq) * 100000 / 16384000;
                Line2Val := INT_TO_DINT(ClearFreq) * 100000 / 16384000;
                Line3Val := INT_TO_DINT(TorqueLimitUp);
                Line4Val := INT_TO_DINT(TorqueLimitDown);

        2: (*MaxJams, HomeFreq, FloorDeadZone, TopDeadZone*)
                (*
                        Line 1: Maximum number of jams in a cycle before a fault is thrown
                        Line 2: Frequency used during homing
                        Line 3: Floor dead zone
                        Line 4: Ceiling dead zone
                *)
                PBoxText(ENABLE := L1Enabled, CLEAR := ClearDisplay, ROW := 0, COLUMN := 0,
                        TEXT := MaxJamsStr);
                PBoxValue(ENABLE := L1Enabled, ROW := 0,
                        VALUE := INT_TO_DINT(MaxJams));
                PBoxText(ENABLE := TRUE, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := 0, COLUMN := 19,
                        TEXT := UpArrowChar);

                PBoxText(ENABLE := L2Enabled, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := 1, COLUMN := 0,
                        TEXT := HomeFreqStr);
                PBoxValue(ENABLE := L2Enabled, ROW := 1,
                        VALUE := INT_TO_DINT(HomeFreq) * 100000 / 16384000);
                PBoxText(ENABLE := TRUE, CLEAR := ClearDisplay, ROW := 1, COLUMN := 18,
                        TEXT := PercentChar);
                PBoxText(ENABLE := TRUE, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := 1, COLUMN := 19,
                        TEXT := MidChar);

                PBoxText(ENABLE := L3Enabled, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := 2, COLUMN := 0,
                        TEXT := FloorDeadZoneStr);
                PBoxValue(ENABLE := L3Enabled, ROW := 2,
                        VALUE := FloorDeadZone);
                PBoxText(ENABLE := TRUE, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := 2, COLUMN := 19,
                        TEXT := MidChar);

                PBoxText(ENABLE := L4Enabled, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := 3, COLUMN := 0,
                        TEXT := TopDeadZoneStr);
                PBoxValue(ENABLE := L4Enabled, ROW := 3,
                        VALUE := TopDeadZone);
                PBoxText(ENABLE := TRUE, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := 3, COLUMN := 19,
                        TEXT := DownArrowChar);

                Line1Val := INT_TO_DINT(MaxJams);
                Line2Val := INT_TO_DINT(HomeFreq) * 100000 / 16384000;
                Line3Val := FloorDeadZone;
                Line4Val := TopDeadZone;

        3: (*HomingTorqueLimit, EndPos, RestTime, JamTime*)
                (*
                        Line 1: Torque limit used to mark the reference point during homing
                        Line 2: End position (ceiling position in millirevolutions)
                        Line 3: Pause duration when the door reaches the ceiling
                        Line 4: Time spent off after encountering a jam going up
                *)
                PBoxText(ENABLE := L1Enabled, CLEAR := ClearDisplay, ROW := 0, COLUMN := 0,
                        TEXT := HomeTorqueLimitStr);
                PBoxValue(ENABLE := L1Enabled, ROW := 0,
                        VALUE := INT_TO_DINT(HomingTorqueLimit));
                PBoxText(ENABLE := TRUE, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := 0, COLUMN := 19,
                        TEXT := UpArrowChar);

                PBoxText(ENABLE := L2Enabled, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := 1, COLUMN := 0,
                        TEXT := EndPosStr);
                PBoxValue(ENABLE := L2Enabled, ROW := 1,
                        VALUE := EndPos);
                PBoxText(ENABLE := TRUE, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := 1, COLUMN := 19,
                        TEXT := MidChar);

                PBoxText(ENABLE := L3Enabled, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := 2, COLUMN := 0,
                        TEXT := RestTimeStr);
                PBoxValue(ENABLE := L3Enabled, ROW := 2,
                        VALUE := RestTime);
                PBoxText(ENABLE := TRUE, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := 2, COLUMN := 19,
                        TEXT := MidChar);

                PBoxText(ENABLE := L4Enabled, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := 3, COLUMN := 0,
                        TEXT := JamTimeStr);
                PBoxValue(ENABLE := L4Enabled, ROW := 3,
                        VALUE := JamTime);
                PBoxText(ENABLE := TRUE, CLEAR := ClearDisplay, ROW := 3, COLUMN := 19,
                        TEXT := DownArrowChar);

                Line1Val := INT_TO_DINT(HomingTorqueLimit);
                Line2Val := EndPos;
                Line3Val := RestTime;
                Line4Val := JamTime;

        4: (*Preset selector - single row*)
                (*
                        Line 1: Preset selector. Loads the selected preset, or saves the
                                currently edited values back into it.
                *)
                PBoxText(ENABLE := L1Enabled, CLEAR := ClearDisplay, ROW := 0, COLUMN := 0,
                        TEXT := ConfigSelectStr);
                PBoxValue(ENABLE := L1Enabled, ROW := 0,
                        VALUE := INT_TO_DINT(ConfigSelect));
                PBoxText(ENABLE := TRUE, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := 0, COLUMN := 19,
                        TEXT := EndChar);

                Line1Val := INT_TO_DINT(ConfigSelect);
ELSE
        IsParBoxOn := TRUE;

        (*Main operating page*)
        PBoxText(ENABLE := TRUE, CLEAR := ClearDisplay, ROW := 0, COLUMN := 0, TEXT := RunPageL0);
        PBoxText(ENABLE := TRUE, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := 1, COLUMN := 0, TEXT := RunPageL1);
        PBoxText(ENABLE := TRUE, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := 2, COLUMN := 0, TEXT := RunPageL2);
        PBoxText(ENABLE := TRUE, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := 3, COLUMN := 0, TEXT := RunPageL0);

        (*Row 3 live position*)
        PBoxValue(ENABLE := TRUE, ROW := 2, COLUMN := 3, POINT := 3, LENGTH := 8,
                VALUE := _145_Actual_pos);
        (*Row 3 current state number*)
        PBoxValue(ENABLE := TRUE, ROW := 2, COLUMN := 16, POINT := BYTE#0, LENGTH := 2,
                VALUE := INT_TO_DINT(State));
END_CASE;

ClearDisplay := FALSE;

(*Parameter page UI*)
IF Page > 0 THEN
        IsParBoxOn := FALSE;

        (*OK key: start or confirm editing. Blocked while a write sequence or homing is active*)
        IF KeyRise.5 AND (ConfigInit = 0) AND (WriterPhase = 0) AND (ParamInit = 0) AND (State <> 0) THEN
                IF NOT IsEditing THEN
                        IsEditing := TRUE;
                        CASE RowIndex OF
                                0: EditBuffer := Line1Val;
                                1: EditBuffer := Line2Val;
                                2: EditBuffer := Line3Val;
                                3: EditBuffer := Line4Val;
                        END_CASE;
                ELSE
                        IsEditing := FALSE;
                        L1Enabled := TRUE;
                        L2Enabled := TRUE;
                        L3Enabled := TRUE;
                        L4Enabled := TRUE;
                        FlashTimer(IN := FALSE);

                        IF Page = 4 THEN
                                (*Preset selector: load and save the selected preset*)
                                IF (EditBuffer >= 1) AND (EditBuffer <= MaxPreset) THEN
                                        ConfigSelect := DINT_TO_INT(EditBuffer);
                                        ConfigInit := 20;
                                END_IF;
                        ELSE
                                (*Percent rows: convert back to 0..16384*)
                                IF ((Page = 1) AND (RowIndex <= 1)) OR ((Page = 2) AND (RowIndex = 1)) THEN
                                        EditBuffer := EditBuffer * DINT#4096 / DINT#25 + DINT#1;
                                END_IF;

                                (*16-bit P355 rows must stay within INT range*)
                                IF (Page < 3) OR (RowIndex = 0) THEN
                                        EditBuffer := MIN(EditBuffer, 32767);
                                END_IF;

                                (*Write only the edited parameter*)
                                SaveOne := TRUE;
                                ConfigInit := RowIndex + 4 * (Page - 1) + 1;
                        END_IF;
                END_IF;
        END_IF;

        (*User is adjusting the selected parameter*)
        IF IsEditing THEN
                (*Up has priority when both keys are held*)
                IF _72_Parameterbox_key_state.3 OR _72_Parameterbox_key_state.4 THEN
                        IF _72_Parameterbox_key_state.3 THEN
                                IF KeyRise.3 THEN
                                        Inc := 0;
                                        IncLvl := 1;
                                        EditBuffer := EditBuffer + 1;
                                END_IF;
                        ELSIF KeyRise.4 THEN
                                Inc := 0;
                                IncLvl := 1;
                                EditBuffer := MAX(EditBuffer - 1, 0);
                        END_IF;

                        IncTimer(IN := TRUE, PT := IncTime);
                        IF IncTimer.Q THEN
                                Inc := Inc + IncLvl;
                                IncTimer(IN := FALSE);
                                IF _72_Parameterbox_key_state.3 THEN
                                        EditBuffer := EditBuffer + INT_TO_DINT(Inc);
                                ELSE
                                        EditBuffer := MAX(EditBuffer - INT_TO_DINT(Inc), 0);
                                END_IF;
                        END_IF;

                        (*Grow the increment the longer the key is held, so long presses move faster*)
                        IF IncLvl MOD 5 = 0 THEN
                                IncLvl := IncLvl * IncLvl * IncLvl + 5;
                        END_IF;
                ELSE
                        IncTimer(IN := FALSE);
                        Inc := 0;
                        IncLvl := 1;
                END_IF;

                (*Clamp the three percentage edit rows; decrement logic already prevents negatives.*)
                IF ((Page = 1) AND (RowIndex <= 1)) OR ((Page = 2) AND (RowIndex = 1)) THEN
                        EditBuffer := MIN(EditBuffer, DINT#100);
                END_IF;

                (*Edited value*)
                PBoxValue(ENABLE := TRUE, ROW := INT_TO_BYTE(RowIndex), COLUMN := 12, POINT := 0, LENGTH := 6,
                        VALUE := EditBuffer);

                (*Flash the parameter name while editing*)
                FlashTimer(IN := NOT FlashTimer.Q, PT := FlashTime);
                IF FlashTimer.Q THEN
                        CASE RowIndex OF
                                0: CurrentLineEnabled := L1Enabled;
                                1: CurrentLineEnabled := L2Enabled;
                                2: CurrentLineEnabled := L3Enabled;
                                3: CurrentLineEnabled := L4Enabled;
                        END_CASE;

                        IF CurrentLineEnabled THEN
                                PBoxText(ENABLE := TRUE, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := INT_TO_BYTE(RowIndex), COLUMN := 1,
                                        TEXT := BlankString);
                        END_IF;
                        CurrentLineEnabled := NOT CurrentLineEnabled;

                        CASE RowIndex OF
                                0: L1Enabled := CurrentLineEnabled;
                                1: L2Enabled := CurrentLineEnabled;
                                2: L3Enabled := CurrentLineEnabled;
                                3: L4Enabled := CurrentLineEnabled;
                        END_CASE;
                END_IF;
        ELSE
                (*Scrolling. Page 4 has one selectable row only; no wrap at either end.*)
                CASE RowIndex OF
                        0:
                                IF ScrollUpEvent AND (Page > 1) THEN
                                        RowIndex := 3;
                                        Page := Page - 1;
                                        ClearDisplay := TRUE;
                                END_IF;
                                IF ScrollDownEvent AND (Page < 4) THEN
                                        RowIndex := 1;
                                END_IF;
                        1, 2:
                                IF ScrollUpEvent THEN
                                        RowIndex := RowIndex - 1;
                                END_IF;
                                IF ScrollDownEvent THEN
                                        RowIndex := RowIndex + 1;
                                END_IF;
                        3:
                                IF ScrollUpEvent THEN
                                        RowIndex := 2;
                                END_IF;
                                IF ScrollDownEvent AND (Page < 4) THEN
                                        RowIndex := 0;
                                        Page := Page + 1;
                                        ClearDisplay := TRUE;
                                END_IF;
                END_CASE;

                FlashTimer(IN := FALSE);
        END_IF;

        (*'>' while scrolling, '*' while editing*)
        IF IsEditing THEN
                PBoxText(ENABLE := TRUE, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := INT_TO_BYTE(RowIndex), COLUMN := 0,
                        TEXT := ModChar);
        ELSE
                PBoxText(ENABLE := TRUE, CLEAR := FALSE, ROW := INT_TO_BYTE(RowIndex), COLUMN := 0,
                        TEXT := SelChar);
        END_IF;
END_IF;

(*5. -----------------------------Drive state machine------------------------------*)
CASE State OF
        0: (*Homing*)
                _39_PLC_set_digital_output_bus.8 := FALSE;
                Power := TRUE;
                IsHoming := TRUE;
                TorqueEdge(CLK := (ABS(_90_Actual_torque_current) > HomingTorqueLimit));

                CASE HomingState OF
                        0: (*Homing begins upwards in the positive direction*)
                                IF DI5Edge.Q
                                OR ((KeyRise.3 OR KeyRise.4 OR KeyRise.5) AND IsParBoxOn)
                                OR (TorqueEdge.Q AND (_90_Actual_torque_current > 0)) THEN
                                        _39_PLC_set_digital_output_bus.8 := TRUE;
                                        EndPos := _145_Actual_pos;
                                        HomingState := 1;
                                END_IF;

                        1: (*Homing ends downwards in the negative direction*)
                                IF DI6Edge.Q
                                OR ((KeyRise.3 OR KeyRise.4 OR KeyRise.5) AND IsParBoxOn)
                                OR (TorqueEdge.Q AND (_90_Actual_torque_current < 0)) THEN
                                        _39_PLC_set_digital_output_bus.8 := TRUE;
                                        EndPos := EndPos - _145_Actual_pos;
                                        IF EndPos < (FloorDeadZone + TopDeadZone) THEN
                                                EndPos := FloorDeadZone + TopDeadZone;
                                        END_IF;

                                        WritePos(EXECUTE := FALSE);
                                        WritePos(
                                                EXECUTE := TRUE,
                                                PARAMETERNUMBER := 356,
                                                PARAMETERINDEX := 1,
                                                VALUE := EndPos,
                                                RAMONLY := 0);

                                        HomingState := 2;
                                END_IF;
                END_CASE;

        1: (*Opening*)
                IF Power AND NOT MoveExecute AND (TargetPos = EndPos) THEN
                        MoveExecute := TRUE;
                END_IF;

                IF (_5_State_digital_input.0 OR (KeyRise.3 AND IsParBoxOn))
                AND NOT (_5_State_digital_input.1 OR (KeyRise.4 AND IsParBoxOn)) THEN
                        TargetPos := EndPos;
                        SetFreq := RunFreq;
                        IF NOT Power THEN
                                MoveExecute := FALSE;
                                Power := TRUE;
                        ELSE
                                MoveExecute := TRUE;
                        END_IF;
                END_IF;

                IF FB_MoveAbs.Done AND ((EndPos - _145_Actual_pos) < TopDeadZone) THEN
                        Power := FALSE;
                        MoveExecute := FALSE;
                        RestTimer(IN := FALSE);
                        State := 2;
                END_IF;

                IF (_5_State_digital_input.1 OR (KeyRise.4 AND IsParBoxOn))
                AND (_145_Actual_pos > (FloorDeadZone * 105 / 100)) THEN
                        RestTimer(IN := FALSE);
                        MoveExecute := FALSE;
                        State := 3;
                END_IF;

        2: (*Reached top*)
                RestTimer(IN := TRUE, PT := RestTime);
                JamCount := 0;

                IF (RestTimer.Q OR _5_State_digital_input.1 OR (KeyRise.4 AND IsParBoxOn))
                AND NOT (_5_State_digital_input.0 OR (_72_Parameterbox_key_state.3 AND IsParBoxOn)) THEN
                        RestTimer(IN := FALSE);
                        MoveExecute := TRUE;
                        State := 3;
                END_IF;

        3: (*Closing*)
                TargetPos := DINT#0;
                SetFreq := RunFreq;
                MoveExecute := TRUE;

                IF _5_State_digital_input.0 OR (KeyRise.3 AND IsParBoxOn) THEN
                        TargetPos := EndPos;
                        MoveExecute := FALSE;
                        State := 1;
                ELSE
                        Power := TRUE;
                END_IF;

                IF FB_MoveAbs.Done AND (_145_Actual_pos < FloorDeadZone) THEN
                        Power := FALSE;
                        IF (NOT _5_State_digital_input.1) OR NOT (KeyRise.4 AND IsParBoxOn) THEN
                                MoveExecute := FALSE;
                                JamCount := 0;
                                Init := FALSE;
                                State := 1;
                        END_IF;
                END_IF;

        4: (*ERROR STATE 1: Clear jam when going down*)
                IF NOT Power THEN
                        Power := TRUE;
                ELSE
                        MoveExecute := TRUE;
                END_IF;

                TargetPos := EndPos;
                SetFreq := ClearFreq;

                IF FB_MoveAbs.Done THEN
                        MoveExecute := FALSE;
                        State := 3;
                END_IF;

        5, 6: (*ERROR STATES 2/3: jam pause, then recover*)
                JamTimer(IN := TRUE, PT := JamTime);
                Power := FALSE;
                MoveExecute := FALSE;

                IF JamTimer.Q THEN
                        IF State = 6 THEN
                                TargetPos := EndPos;
                                SetFreq := ClearFreq;
                        END_IF;
                        Power := TRUE;
                        MoveExecute := TRUE;

                        IF State = 5 THEN
                                JamTimer(IN := FALSE);
                                State := 1;
                        ELSIF FB_MoveAbs.Done THEN
                                JamTimer(IN := FALSE);
                                MoveExecute := FALSE;
                                State := 3;
                        END_IF;
                END_IF;
END_CASE;

(*6. ------------------------------Fault clearing-----------------------------------*)
IF _72_Parameterbox_key_state.1 THEN
        _110_ErrorFlags.0 := FALSE;
        _110_ErrorFlags.1 := FALSE;
        _110_ErrorFlags.2 := FALSE;

        FB_MoveAbs(EXECUTE := FALSE);
        Power := TRUE;
        IsHoming := FALSE;
        MoveExecute := FALSE;

        Init := FALSE;
        JamCount := 0;
        State := 1;
END_IF;

IF JamCount >= MaxJams THEN
        _110_ErrorFlags.0 := TRUE;
END_IF;

FB_Reset(EXECUTE := _72_Parameterbox_key_state.1);

(*7. ------------------------------Homing handling--------------------------------------*)
IF _72_Parameterbox_key_state.0 AND _72_Parameterbox_key_state.5 AND IsParBoxOn
AND (State = 1) AND (_88_Current_speed = 0) THEN
        Power := TRUE;
        HomingState := 0;
        IsHoming := TRUE;
        State := 0;
        MoveExecute := FALSE;
END_IF;

IF FB_Home.Done OR FB_Home.Error THEN
        IsHoming := FALSE;
        MoveExecute := FALSE;
        Power := FALSE;
        Init := FALSE;
        State := 1;
END_IF;

(*8. -----------------------------Movement, power and current position saving------------------------*)
FB_Power(ENABLE := Power);
(* Do not reset Init continuously at the floor. That re-ran ParamInit every scan,
   preventing it completing and blocking ParameterBox saves. *)

IF FB_Power.Status THEN
        FB_MoveAbs(
                EXECUTE := MoveExecute AND Power AND NOT IsHoming,
                POSITION := TargetPos,
                VELOCITY := SetFreq,
                MODE := 0
        );

        FB_Home(EXECUTE := IsHoming,
                POSITION := 0,
                VELOCITY := HomeFreq,
                MODE := 16
        );
END_IF;
]]></Program><Checksum>F2E2BA53078300948EE5DA6D89710A867117E6533E82F5BFFCB6DF90</Checksum></PLCFile></NordCon>
